                 background-color: #F8F8F8;\n                        }\n                    \n            .ot-floating-button__front{background-image:url('https://cdn.cookielaw.org/logos/static/ot_persistent_cookie_icon.png')}\n                      @keyframes slide-down-custom {\n                          0% {\n                              bottom: 720px !important;\n                          }\n                          100% {\n                              bottom: 0px;\n                          }\n                      }\n                      @-webkit-keyframes slide-down-custom {\n                          0% {\n                              bottom: 720px !important;\n                          }\n                          100% {\n                              bottom: 0px;\n                          }\n                      }\n                      @-moz-keyframes slide-down-custom {\n                          0% {\n                              bottom: 720px !important;\n                          }\n                          100% {\n                              bottom: 0px;\n                          }\n                      } In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > HR Generalist - Talent and Systems Central College Apply HR Generalist - Talent and Systems PELLA, IA Apply Job Type Full-time Description The Human Resource Generalist - Talent and Systems position supports a broad range of HR functions with focus on talent acquisition, employee development, HR processes, and HRIS administration.  The role serves as a resource to employees and leaders throughout the employee lifecycle by ensuring HR systems, processes and practices are accurate and aligned with organizational needs.  The ideal candidate is highly organized, relationship-oriented, and comfortable balancing people-focused responsibilities with technology, data, and process management. Job responsibilities: Coordinate and support the full recruitment and onboarding processes while maintaining accurate records of employment documentation. Provide consultative support to supervisors and campus leaders on employee lifecycle, talent management, performance, and HR policy matters. Support talent management initiatives across campus and in all stages of the employee lifecycle. Assist with performance management, employee development, career planning, and succession planning processes. Help maintain and grow programs designed to support employee engagement, retention, and development. Respond to employee concerns, workplace issues, and policy questions; assist with investigations and conflict resolution as appropriate to ensure consistent application and administration of policies. Collaborate with HR colleagues, campus leaders, payroll, benefits, IT, and other stakeholders to ensure effective and consistent delivery of HR services. Serve as key administrator of HRIS and related systems to ensure maintenance of accurate employee, position, and organizational data. Generate and maintain reports to support campus functions and to complete data surveys as required. Provide systems support and resources for employees and supervisors and drive process improvements to continue to better support campus needs. Maintain confidentiality of employee and college information while handling sensitive situations with a high level of discretion. Ensure compliance with all applicable federal, state, and local employment laws and regulations. Requirements Bachelor's degree preferred in business, management, human resources, or related field with 2-5 years of effective experience. PHR/SHRM-CP certification preferred. Previous HRIS database applications experience with proficiency in report writing tools preferred. Paylocity experience a plus. Strong organizational, communication, attention to detail and data analysis skills required. Ability to build effective working relationships with employees, supervisors, and senior leaders required. Strong knowledge of employment law, policies, and regulations required. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Paylocity Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy SMS Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookies Settings Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Back Button Performance Cookies Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest Switch Label label Switch Label label Switch Label label Reject All Confirm My Choices"
