    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4433720/Central-College/Grounds-Technician": {
      "title": "Grounds Technician",
      "description": "Central College - Grounds Technician In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Grounds Technician Central College Apply Grounds Technician PELLA, IA • Facilities Management Apply Job Type Full-time Description Responsible to the Grounds Manager for performing a variety of grounds and general maintenance tasks. · Responsible for mowing, trimming, weeding, seeding, landscaping, planting, watering, and snow removal. · Assist with fertilizer and pesticide application (if licensed and certified). · Operate grounds equipment i.e., tractors, mowers, spreaders, push mowers, snow blowers according to safety requirements and guidelines. · Assist with basic maintenance of grounds equipment and other general maintenance tasks.. · Complete deliveries, office and furniture moves and resident housing bed bunking based on needs and project assignments · Support event set-up/tear down on campus/athletic grounds and in campus facilities. · Maintain clean shops and mechanical rooms. · Assist facilities staff with projects and tasks as needed Requirements · High School Diploma/GED and must be able to do simple math functions. · 1 year of effective experience and valid driver’s license required. · Ability to use/climb a ladder safely and lift, push & pull up to 100 pounds. · Must be able to work flexible hours for snow removal duties or other special events as needed Central Brand Expectations: · Demonstrate a network of caring relationships by showing respect for others, being dependable and promoting cooperation with others in the work environment. · Be your best self by being accountable for responsibilities, adapting well to change and maintaining the highest standards of business ethics. · Perform job responsibilities on campus to support the residential college environment. · Strive to perform as effectively as possible while maintaining a high level of quality and promoting personal growth and development. · Respect and comply with college rules and policies, including participation in required training courses; report any suspected violations of the Title IX policy to the Title IX Coordinator. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Paylocity Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy SMS Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy"
    },
