    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4590702/Central-College/Campus-Safety-Associate": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Associate",
      "description": "Central College - Campus Safety Associate In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Campus Safety Associate Central College Apply Campus Safety Associate PELLA, IA • Campus Information and Postal Services Apply Job Type Full-time Description The Campus Safety Associate plays a key role in maintaining a safe and secure environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors on campus. Responds to evening and overnight concerns, while knowing College resources and who to delegate the concerns for a timely and appropriate response.  This position focuses primarily on weeknight coverage, Tuesday through Thursday, 7:00 PM – 7:00 AM. An excellent schedule for individuals looking to maintain open weekends. Weekend coverage may be required on an exceptional or rotating basis. Lock and unlock campus buildings according to set schedule and events schedule. Respond to emergency situations routed through the information center and forward messages to the appropriate individual. Respond to fire and other mechanical alarms. Basic facilities knowledge of plumbing and electrical safety. Performs routine and preventative maintenance. Assist with parking enforcement and reserved parking. Have thorough understanding and knowledge of campus resources. Maintain an appropriate level of professionalism and confidentiality. Central College Brand Expectations : Demonstrate a network of caring relationships by showing respect for others, being dependable and promoting cooperation with others in the work environment. Be your best self by being accountable for responsibilities, adapting well to change and maintaining the highest standards of business ethics. Perform job responsibilities on campus to support the residential college environment. Strive to perform as effectively as possible while maintaining a high level of quality and promoting personal growth and development. Respect and comply with college rules and policies, including participation in required training courses; report any suspected violations of the Title IX policy to the Title IX Coordinator. Requirements High School Diploma Excellent customer services skills Ability to work with students, faculty and staff representing diverse backgrounds and interests. Ability to work independently Weekend coverage may be required on an exceptional or rotating basis. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Paylocity Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy SMS Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4590425/Central-College/Retail-Management-Office-Assistant": {
      "title": "Retail Management Office Assistant",
      "description": "Central College - Retail Management Office Assistant In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Retail Management Office Assistant Central College Apply Retail Management Office Assistant PELLA, IA • Retail Management Apply Job Type Part-time Description Office administration: Manage routine correspondence, maintain departmental records, order office supplies, and organize shared files, forms, and calendars. Customer service: Serve as an initial contact for students, employees, families, vendors, and community guests; answer routine questions and direct requests to the appropriate manager. Financial support: Prepare invoices, process purchasing paperwork, organize receipts, assist with sales and deposit reconciliation, and track outstanding payments in coordination with the Business Office. Reporting and data entry: Compile sales, attendance, meal plan, and expense information; maintain spreadsheets; and prepare routine reports for management review. Dining and meal plan support: Assist with meal plan inquiries, account updates, departmental charges, and Big Red Bucks administration within established procedures and access permissions. Event Services support: Enter event inquiries, maintain booking information, prepare approved estimates and confirmations, and coordinate administrative details with event staff. Retail and cinema support: Assist with purchase orders, inventory records, merchandise information, group booking inquiries, and promotional schedules. Communications: Maintain accurate operating hours, service information, menus, and announcements across approved communication channels; coordinate updates with managers and Communications. Records and compliance support: Track required vendor documents, agreements, and renewal dates, referring items requiring approval to the appropriate manager. Team support: Identify opportunities to improve administrative processes, provide support during peak periods, and model a professional, service-focused approach. Central College Brand Expectations: Demonstrate a network of caring relationships by showing respect for others, being dependable and promoting cooperation with others in the work environment. Be your best self by being accountable for responsibilities, adapting well to change and maintaining the highest standards of business ethics. Perform job responsibilities on campus to support the residential college environment. Strive to perform as effectively as possible while maintaining a high level of quality and promoting personal growth and development. Respect and comply with college rules and policies, including participation in required training courses; report any suspected violations of the Title IX policy to the Title IX Coordinator. Requirements Must be able to add, subtract, multiply, and divide to include working with decimals and fractions. 1 to 3 years of effective experience required Apply View All Jobs Powered by Paylocity Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy SMS Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy"
    },
